{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-39287-r4513695","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Rice with Tofu and Nuts","sourcePageId":39287,"sourceRevision":"4513695","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:10:25Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Rice%20with%20Tofu%20and%20Nuts&oldid=4513695","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:23.524Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using cashew","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using nuts and seeds","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using tofu","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Side dish recipes","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"40156dbb6955783d98bd3b4030675e98b91d00d14aa400010b5295229f51bf48","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Servings = 1–2\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Vegan cuisine|Vegan Cuisine]]\n\nThis recipe serves 1 person as a main dish and 2 people as a side dish.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (120 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) Basmati [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 1 cup (240 g) [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] firm [[Cookbook:Tofu|tofu]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Olive oil|olive oil]]\n* 2 tbsp blanched slivered [[Cookbook:Almond|almonds]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashews]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Pepper|peppercorns]]\n* 1-inch piece [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]] stick\n* 2 whole [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 2 cups (480 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) water\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Wash the rice with several changes of cold water. Drain. \n# Add the water, bay leaf, peppercorns, cinnamon, cloves and salt and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. \n# Reduce heat to medium low and cook covered for about 12 minutes until all the water has evaporated and the rice grains are tender yet separate. \n# Heat the oil in a pan. \n# Add the tofu and shallow-[[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] until for a few minutes on each side. \n# Scoop out of the oil and set aside. \n# To the same oil, add the nuts and the raisins and shallow-fry until the nuts are golden brown and the raisins have plumped up.\n# Remove from heat.\n# Turn the rice into a serving bowl and fluff gently with a fork. \n# Fold in the tofu and the nuts gently and mix well. \n# Serve hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* The whole spices are intended to be discarded, not eaten.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using tofu]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nuts and seeds]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Rice with Tofu and Nuts","nameAr":null,"servings":nul